text: ['Artifact spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.', 'As Adaptive Automaton enters the battlefield, choose a creature type.\\nAdaptive Automaton is the chosen type in addition to its other types.\\nOther creatures you control of the chosen type get +1/+1.', "As Caged Sun enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\nCreatures you control of the chosen color get +1/+1.\\nWhenever a land's ability causes you to add one or more mana of the chosen color, add one additional mana of that color.", 'As Cloud Key enters the battlefield, choose artifact, creature, enchantment, instant, or sorcery.\\nSpells you cast of the chosen type cost {1} less to cast.', 'As Phyrexian Processor enters the battlefield, pay any amount of life.\\n{4}, {T}: Create an X/X black Phyrexian Minion creature token, where X is the life paid as Phyrexian Processor entered the battlefield.', "As Phyrexian Revoker enters the battlefield, choose a nonland card name.\\nActivated abilities of sources with the chosen name can't be activated.", 'Astral Cornucopia enters the battlefield with X charge counters on it.\\n{T}: Choose a color. Add one mana of that color for each charge counter on Astral Cornucopia.', "At the beginning of combat on your turn, create a token that's a copy of equipped creature, except the token isn't legendary. That token gains haste.\\nEquip {5}", "At the beginning of each player's draw step, if Howling Mine is untapped, that player draws an additional card.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you gain X life, where X is the number of cards in your hand minus 4.', 'Deathtouch, lifelink\\nWhen Wurmcoil Engine dies, create a 3/3 colorless Phyrexian Wurm artifact creature token with deathtouch and a 3/3 colorless Phyrexian Wurm artifact creature token with lifelink.', 'Door to Nothingness enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{W}{W}{U}{U}{B}{B}{R}{R}{G}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Door to Nothingness: Target player loses the game.', "Each spell costs {3} more to cast except during its controller's turn.", 'Equipped creature gets +1/+0.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Equipped creature gets +1/+1 for each land you control.\\nEquip legendary creature {3}\\nEquip {7}', 'Equipped creature gets +1/+2.\\nEquip {2}\\nWhenever a 1/1 creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may return Sword of the Meek from your graveyard to the battlefield, then attach it to that creature.', 'Equipped creature has deathtouch.\\nWhenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, that player loses half their life, rounded up.\\nEquip {3}', 'Equipped creature has first strike and gets +X/+0, where X is the number of instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard.\\nEquip {2}', "Equipped creature has hexproof and haste. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nEquip {1}", 'Flying', "Flying\\nWhenever you cast a spell, put a +1/+1 counter on Ramos, Dragon Engine for each of that spell's colors.\\nRemove five +1/+1 counters from Ramos: Add {W}{W}{U}{U}{B}{B}{R}{R}{G}{G}. Activate only once each turn.", "Flying\\nYou can't lose the game and your opponents can't win the game.", 'Imprint — When Semblance Anvil enters the battlefield, you may exile a nonland card from your hand.\\nSpells you cast that share a card type with the exiled card cost {2} less to cast.', 'Lands you control have "{T}: Add one mana of any color."\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Nonartifact spells cost {1} more to cast.', "Nonartifact spells you cast have improvise. (Your artifacts can help cast those spells. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)", 'Noncreature spells cost {1} more to cast.', "Psychosis Crawler's power and toughness are each equal to the number of cards in your hand.\\nWhenever you draw a card, each opponent loses 1 life.", 'Sacrifice a creature: Add {C}{C}.', "Sacrifice a creature: Target player mills cards equal to the sacrificed creature's power.", "Untap all artifacts you control during each other player's untap step.", 'When Elsewhere Flask enters the battlefield, draw a card.\\nSacrifice Elsewhere Flask: Choose a basic land type. Each land you control becomes that type until end of turn.', 'When Ichor Wellspring enters the battlefield or is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Precursor Golem enters the battlefield, create two 3/3 colorless Golem artifact creature tokens.\\nWhenever a player casts an instant or sorcery spell that targets only a single Golem, that player copies that spell for each other Golem that spell could target. Each copy targets a different one of those Golems.', 'When Self-Assembler enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an Assembly-Worker creature card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "When Soul-Guide Lantern enters the battlefield, exile target card from a graveyard.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Soul-Guide Lantern: Exile each opponent's graveyard.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Soul-Guide Lantern: Draw a card.", 'When Sundering Titan enters or leaves the battlefield, choose a land of each basic land type, then destroy those lands.', 'Whenever Scrap Trawler or another artifact you control is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, return to your hand target artifact card in your graveyard with lesser mana value.', "Whenever a permanent becomes untapped, that permanent's controller mills a card.", 'Whenever an opponent draws a card, you may pay {1}. If you do, draw a card.', 'Whenever equipped creature attacks alone, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each other creature you control.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', "Whenever you cast a spell, you gain 1 life for each spell you've cast this turn.\\nPay 50 life: Aetherflux Reservoir deals 50 damage to any target.", 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {X}, where X is less than or equal to the amount of life you gained. If you do, draw X cards.', 'You may have Sculpting Steel enter the battlefield as a copy of any artifact on the battlefield.', 'You may look at the top card of your library any time.\\nYou may cast artifact spells and colorless spells from the top of your library.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Exile the top card of your library.', '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Chromatic Star: Add one mana of any color.\\nWhen Chromatic Star is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', '{1}: Untap Staff of Domination.\\n{2}, {T}: You gain 1 life.\\n{3}, {T}: Untap target creature.\\n{4}, {T}: Tap target creature.\\n{5}, {T}: Draw a card.', '{2}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{2}, {T}: Target player mills two cards.', '{3}, Sacrifice Burnished Hart: Search your library for up to two basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{3}, {T}: Reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a land card. Goblin Charbelcher deals damage equal to the number of nonland cards revealed this way to any target. If the revealed land card was a Mountain, Goblin Charbelcher deals double that damage instead. Put the revealed cards on the bottom of your library in any order.', '{3}, {T}: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', '{4}, {T}: You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield.', '{5}, {T}, Exile Perilous Vault: Exile all nonland permanents.', "{5}, {T}: Target player mills X cards, where X is the number of cards in that player's graveyard.", "{T}, Discard a card: Up to one target creature can't be blocked this turn.\\nWhenever Key to the City becomes untapped, you may pay {2}. If you do, draw a card.", '{T}, Put a page counter on Mazemind Tome: Scry 1.\\n{2}, {T}, Put a page counter on Mazemind Tome: Draw a card.\\nWhen there are four or more page counters on Mazemind Tome, exile it. If you do, you gain 4 life.', "{T}, Sacrifice Mishra's Bauble: Look at the top card of target player's library. Draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", '{T}, Tap an untapped creature you control: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color among legendary creatures and planeswalkers you control.', '{T}: Add three mana of any one color.', '{T}: Add {C}. You gain 1 life.', '{T}: Target permanent becomes an artifact in addition to its other types until end of turn.']
flavor: ['"A crystallized moment in time from the Mending Era, first discovered during the Ice Age. A temporal conundrum, even to the great scholar himself."\\n—*The Discoveries of Feldon*', '"A key only unlocks a door. Its wielder must choose whether to cross the threshold."\\n—*Hurkyl\'s Metaphysics, vol. II*', '"A rakalite core paired with a powerstone matrix has significantly increased the healing effects of my original amulet design."\\n—Urza, research notes', '"A wish can be controlled. Dreams are far more chaotic, and ungoverned by rationale."\\n—*Hurkyl\'s Metaphysics, vol. II*', '"Arcum is a babbling fool! Phyrexian technology is our greatest blessing. Take this delightful trinket for instance . . ."\\n—Heidar, Rimewind master', '"As the years passed, Urza turned his focus from the Thran to worlds beyond his own, seeking any spell or technology that might break the Phyrexian scourge."\\n—*Urza: From Prodigy to Planeswalker*', '"Based on his early work with primal clay, Tawnos refined the rare metals in the earth into self-assembling strands."\\n—*After the War*', '"Blood fluting needs to be deeper.\\nAdditional hooks needed for nerve\\nrigging. Surface stippling could be coarser.\\n—Ashnod, design notes', '"Delicate resonance detectors could scan the assembly lines for metallic impurities, loose bolts, and freak occurrences of sentience."\\n—Tawnos, proposal for overseer prototype', '"Even if we defeat it, what remains to be saved?"\\n—Glissa Sunseeker', '"Feldon\'s latest discovery appears to draw upon the same \'memories of the land\' my wife studied. How I wish she could see it."\\n—Writings of Drafna', '"From the clouds, you can see as far as the distant horizon. It\'s a reminder of the infinite possibilities of everyday life."\\n—Noboru, master kitemaker', '"Give the schematic to the younger brother. Tell him that it will surely keep Argoth\'s resources out of Urza\'s hands."\\n—Gix, Yawgmoth praetor', '"Harmonic resonance infusions amplify the natural abilities of the song mages of Sumifa."\\n—Drafna, research notes', '"Heat from the rotating mechanism is captured and converted into energy, allowing it to operate in perpetuity."\\n—*Rusko\'s Compendium of Clockwork*', '"I have re-created a Thran portal at last! Before I inform Lord Urza, I\'ll test it myself."\\n—Oryan, Urzan artificer, final research note', '"I now believe the strange orb was some kind of Thran security device. Supporting this theory, I can no longer recall where I found it."\\n—Tocasia, journal entry', '"I sit and I think of Lat-Nam, of the azure waves white with froth, suspended over the shore. I see the energy there and I call it here."\\n—Hurkyl, meditation notes', '"Ideas drift like petals on the wind. I have only to lift my face to the breeze."', '"If powerstones are energy stored in material form, could we store matter as energy in the same way?"\\n—Rayne, research notes', '"If that brain can\'t figure out the secret of the serum, then add more brains."\\n—Rhmir, Hand of the Augur', '"If you work at sawing up carcasses, you notice how the joints fit, how the nerves are arrayed, and how the skin peels back."\\n—Ashnod, to Tawnos', '"In the early days, Urza\'s wondrous automatons were seen as symbols of hope and courage."\\n—*The Antiquities War*', '"In the lean months, communities lived off a bitterwheat berry so tough that its flour contained more millstone than grain."\\n—*On the Early History of Keld*', '"It is neither the species of leaf nor the thickness of branch that creates music. Gaea\'s song is already in the drum."\\n—Gamelen, Citanul elder', '"It is not that you will go mad. It is that you will beg for madness."\\n—Volrath', '"Measure the angles carefully. Note the gauge of the paper. By your sixth birthday, I expect a flying prototype."\\n—Tawnos, letter to Harbin', '"My dreams have brought more visions from our master: an altar, exquisite and perfect. We must build it at once."\\n—Writings of Artonac, priest of Gix', '"My husband is clever enough to bottle the sky, and foolish enough to ignore its beauty."\\n—Queen Kayla bin-Kroog', '"Our glorious infection has taken hold."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"Perhaps drawing the impossible monster will lessen the burden my memory must bear."\\n—Jarsyl, diary', '"Presented to the Chief Artificer in recognition of his unparalleled service to Yotia."\\n—Rusted plaque', '"Progress update: the problem of the slagheap blocking the entrance seems to have solved itself."\\n—Mine supervisor\'s report', '"Properly installed, each powerstone emits a targeted electromagnetic field that halts momentum as sure as stone."\\n—*Tome of Obstructions*', '"Ringed by white stone, Terisia was a city of scholarship and knowledge, where magic promised a brighter future to a world devoured by artifice."\\n—*The Antiquities War*', '"Serra built angels from the spirits of fallen warriors, but I believe a more mundane power source might suffice."\\n—Karn', '"Should a single drop take hold, the oil begins to consume organic tissue and will multiply until it overwhelms the host."\\n—Yawgmoth, collected writings', '"Somehow it warps the Æther. It brings a strange weight, a blockade in the flow of spellcraft."\\n—Noyan Dar, Tazeem lullmage', '"Tempered in the blood of ten thousand sacrifices? Superstitious drivel."\\n—Mishra, note to his researchers', '"Test 12: Boots now protect wearer from all hazards except blisters. Need to source better insoles."\\n—Development log of Willa, Yotian artificer', '"Test 37: Sentience module is still too strong. It\'s adding ears again."\\n—Development log of Willa, Yotian artificer', '"The Sardian dwarves have let superstition override common sense. There\'s plenty of ore left in the mountain, and we mustn\'t let it go to waste."\\n—Last dispatch of Bolgon, Argivian surveyor', '"The forges consumed all and still screamed for more."\\n—*The Antiquities War*', '"The geode must be mined in moonlight and broken open by a silver hammer."\\n—*Tome of Obstructions*', '"The lotus is a potent but ephemeral source of power. To preserve its potency, lacquer carefully with a conductive coating."\\n—*Hurkyl\'s Metaphysics, vol. II*', '"The music is in the drum. I simply coax it out to be heard."', '"The natural world has already solved our problems. Our challenge is to replicate the elegance of its solutions."\\n—Tawnos', '"The new prototype utilizing a rotational axis is marvelously effective: it makes me want to tear my own ears off."\\n—Ashnod, to her assistants', '"The partisans have unearthed a strange artifact. None know its origin, but it gives them hope of a life beyond."\\n—Elspeth\'s journal', '"The perfection of the lotus reminds me of my hopes for this world . . . and my failures. I will not rest until I\'ve atoned for them."\\n—Karn', '"The secrets of my great-uncle\'s heirloom lie in the world where it was forged: the grease-stained wastes of Phyrexia."\\n—Jarsyl, diary', '"There is great wisdom in rushing headlong into combat . . . if you\'re prepared."\\n—Kenjek, captain of the Thousand Swords', '"These estimates are conservative. Its true capacity may be far, far greater."\\n—Research notes, signature illegible', '"These glyphs describe a Thran device capable of controlling a machine army, but the dimensions make no sense. It\'s nearly the size of the Null Moon."\\n—Urza, diary', '"These skittering creatures were created to hunt the one true threat to Phyrexia: dissent."\\n—Venser, journal', '"They\'ll soon become accustomed to wearing skin that is not their own."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"This war will be over quickly, so we can afford to make the medals out of gold."\\n—Dispatch from the Merchant Council of Korlis', '"To be in the presence of a revoker is to be truly alone."\\n—Kara Vrist, Neurok agent', '"Tools and artisans can be destroyed, but the act of creation is inviolate."\\n—Elspeth Tirel', '"We\'ve had a breakthrough on the fifth iteration. The subject\'s skin was entirely replaced within an hour, and he survived a full day after that!"\\n—Ashnod, to Mishra', '"When metal instruments are scarce, a saw constructed from the subject\'s femur will suffice for a craniectomy."\\n—Ashnod, research notes', '"Without Urza\'s ingenuity, the wings\\nwould never have borne weight. Without\\nMishra\'s courage, we would never have\\nknown the machine\'s true potential. I hope this persuades them to work together more."\\n—Tocasia, journal entry', 'A moment in time made tangible, it has the power to realize epic visions.', 'A step in one direction is two steps away from another.', 'An artificer once dropped one in a vault full of coins. She has yet to find it.', 'As it spins, dead voices shriek in an ever-increasing cacophony, rending the mind asunder.', "As sharp as its bearer's words of faith.", "Automaton inspectors ensure that the Consulate's stringent standards for mass production are upheld.", 'By guild tradition, any puddle of multicolored light on the cobblestones can serve as neutral ground.', 'Forged by divine hands to wander mortal realms.', 'Forged from what it forges.', "Ghirapur's most celebrated inventors have been immortalized in clockwork.", 'In a world where death is always violent, cruel weapons are as common as rocks.', 'It lights up the sky, beckoning enemies only to repel them.', 'It sees itself in all of its creations.', "It spilled the blood of one elder dragon. In Gideon's hands, it may yet taste another's.", 'It would be unfortunate if the key fell into the wrong hands.', "Minds, like mountains, are never so grand and mighty that they can't be reduced to dust.", 'Mined from a cave in the Dark Meanders, it shines brightest when no one is looking.', 'Most books simply deliver knowledge. This one expects some in return.', 'Once a year, the skies over Paliano fill with the flying machines of those who hope to be taken on as pupils by the artificer Muzzio.', 'One night Oona bottled the sky. The next night she aligned the stars and released it.', 'Only a monster could create such a door. Only a fool would open it.', "She is the apex of the artificer's craft, the spirit of the divine called out of base metal.", "Some say the knowledge lost during the Ritual of Rebuking is returned through the well's waters.", "The mine's riches never end, nor do the moans of the spirits doomed to haunt them.", 'The musical sound of its turning triggers the tumblers of revelation.', 'The spirit dragon Ugin arranged the hedrons of Zendikar to direct leylines of energy. To disrupt one is to unleash devastation and chaos.', 'Those who examine the amulet too closely have been known to become part of its ornate carvings.', 'Valuing scholarship above all else, the inhabitants of the Ivory Tower reward those who sacrifice power for knowledge.', "While most power is used for ordinary, everyday tasks, one shouldn't underestimate its potential for the extraordinary.", 'With each honor he earns, Gideon paves the path to his redemption.']
artist: ['Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Ben Hill', 'Ben Thompson', 'Brad Rigney', 'Brom', 'Carl Frank', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chuck Lukacs', 'Cliff Childs', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Astruga', 'David Martin', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Greg Staples', 'Grzegorz Rutkowski', 'Heather Hudson', 'Hiro Izawa', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Irina Nordsol', 'Isis', 'Jakub Kasper', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Chan', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jerry Tiritilli', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'Joseph Meehan', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Kirsten Zirngibl', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Mark Brill', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Mike Bierek', 'Ovidio Cartagena', 'Pete Venters', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Sam Burley', 'Scott Chou', 'Sean Murray', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Stephan Martiniere', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Titus Lunter', 'Toraji', 'Trevor Hairsine', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Warren Mahy', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Zack Stella']
